     cmake -H. -Bbuild -G "Ninja" -DGLEXT_INCLUDE_DIR=\path\to\glext -DPIGLIT_USE_WAFFLE=TRUE -DWaffle_INCLUDE_DIRS=\path\to\waffle\include\waffle -DWaffle_LDFLAGS=\path\to\waffle\lib\libwaffle-1.dll.a
 
 
+### 2.6 RenkuOS / Haiku
+
+The native port uses GLUT and the OpenGL Kit. CMake identifies RenkuOS as
+`Haiku` and selects desktop OpenGL tests with native GLUT by default.
+
+With GCC, `haiku_devel`, `mesa_devel` and `libpng16_devel` installed, install
+the remaining build dependencies:
+
+    pkgman install -y cmake ninja python3.10 numpy_python310 mako_python310 glu_devel
+
+From the source directory, build and install into a private directory:
+
+    cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja \
+        -DPYTHON_EXECUTABLE=/system/bin/python3.10 \
+        -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/boot/home/piglit
+    cmake --build build -j4
+    cmake --install build
+
+Run the installed copy so binaries, generated shaders and profiles are all
+found together. The following commands also work after relocating that
+installation to another directory:
+
+    python3.10 /boot/home/piglit/bin/piglit run -1 --timeout 30 sanity /boot/home/piglit-results/sanity
+    python3.10 /boot/home/piglit/bin/piglit summary console -s /boot/home/piglit-results/sanity
+
+For a full desktop OpenGL run, use the `opengl` profile:
+
+    python3.10 /boot/home/piglit/bin/piglit run -1 --timeout 300 opengl /boot/home/piglit-results/opengl
+
+The `spec/!opengl 1.1/glinfo` result records the actual renderer, OpenGL and
+GLSL versions. Check it when testing an N100 driver: `llvmpipe` and `softpipe`
+identify CPU rendering. Piglit uses whichever renderer the OpenGL Kit selects;
+this port does not force software rendering.
+
+Preserve a results directory from each driver version. To compare runs:
+
+    python3.10 /boot/home/piglit/bin/piglit summary console -s /boot/home/piglit-results/before /boot/home/piglit-results/after
+
+This backend exercises native desktop OpenGL. GLX, WGL, Waffle, EGL, OpenGL ES,
+and DMA-BUF tests are disabled by default. Native GLUT cannot request a core
+profile or multisampled default framebuffer; tests requiring those context
+types report skips. Tests still check their own advertised version and
+extension requirements when the optional `wflinfo` tool is absent.
+
+
 ## 3. How to run tests
 
 Make sure that everything is set up correctly:
